2. The Entity (Storing as JSON)
If you are using a modern DB (like Oracle 19c or PostgreSQL), you can store the payload as a JSON type. If not, we use a Clob but tell Jackson to handle the conversion automatically using an AttributeConverter.
File: com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.model.CommonRequest.java
@Entity
@Table(name = "COMMON_REQUEST")
@Getter @Setter
public class CommonRequest {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String requestType; // "LHO_TRANSFER"
    
    // This tells JPA to convert the DTO to a JSON String for the DB automatically
    @Convert(converter = JpaJsonConverter.class)
    @Column(name = "PAYLOAD", columnDefinition = "CLOB")
    private LhoPayloadDto payload; 
    
    private String targetId;
    private String status;
}

3. The Service Implementation (Handling the Map to DTO)
When you generate the summary, you now map your Map<String, BigDecimal> into the LhoPayloadDto structure before saving.
File: com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.service.CommonMasterServiceImpl.java
@Override
@Transactional
public CommonRequest createLhoTransferRequest(LhoRequestWrapperDto wrapper) {
    
    // 1. Transform the circleWiseDetails from the summary logic
    List<CircleWiseDetailDto> details = wrapper.getPayload().getCircleWiseDetails();
    
    // 2. Build the structured Payload
    LhoPayloadDto payload = LhoPayloadDto.builder()
            .batchId(wrapper.getPayload().getBatchId())
            .processDate(wrapper.getPayload().getProcessDate())
            .totalAmount(wrapper.getPayload().getTotalAmount())
            .totalRecordCount(details.size())
            .circleWiseDetails(details)
            .build();

    // 3. Create the Entity
    CommonRequest request = new CommonRequest();
    request.setRequestType("LHO_TRANSFER");
    request.setPayload(payload); // Set the object directly
    request.setTargetId(payload.getBatchId());
    request.setStatus("P");

    return commonRequestRepository.save(request);
}

4. The Response Handling (Search API)
When your Search API runs, Jackson will now see that payload is an object, not a String, and will produce the clean output you wanted:
Current Output (Wrong):
"payload": "{\"batchId\":\"BATCH-001\"...}"
New Output (Correct):
"payload": {
    "batchId": "BATCH-2026-001",
    "processDate": "2026-02-18",
    "circleWiseDetails": [...]
}

Why this is the correct Backend fix:
 * Strict Typing: By using LhoPayloadDto, you prevent garbage data from entering your PAYLOAD column.
 * Automatic Serialization: You don't need to manually call objectMapper.writeValueAsString(). Spring/Jackson handles the nesting for you.
 * High Precision: Using BigDecimal in the CircleWiseDetailDto ensures that your 20-digit numbers with 4 decimals are preserved exactly as they move from the Service to the Database.
